title: 'statement-store: release a reserved DHT peer before disconnect'
doc:
- audience: Node Dev
  description: |-
    On the v2 DHT path a peer that exceeds the statement rate limit is now released from the
    statement protocol's reserved set before it is disconnected, whether or not it has the DHT
    path. The litep2p peerset ignores a disconnect of a reserved peer, so a DHT peer that steering
    held reserved stayed connected and the rest of its batch was lost.

    Peer steering then pauses the peer for 5 minutes: it leaves the peer unreserved, gives its
    place to the next candidate, and the handler rejects its inbound substream. When the pause
    ends the peer is an ordinary candidate again.
crates:
- name: sc-network-statement
  bump: patch
